                <pb facs="1181" n="1049" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg1049"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/651: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-23T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23,
                                1926—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Your No. 24, January 13, 9 p.m., and No. 35, January 20, 7 p.m. Department
                    awaits with interest results of informal conversations which you have had with
                    Saburi and in the meantime should Japanese Embassy here revive question
                    Department will take stand suggested by you in paragraph 9 of your No. 24.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
